      "clip_id": "E-0017",
      "approved_description": "Event: Corner kick.\nImage 10 shows a dark-shirted player approaching a stationary ball in the\ncorner arc beside the corner flag, where the goal line meets the touchline.\nImages 4 and 9 show dark-shirted attackers and white-shirted defenders\npositioned around the penalty area. Images 11-13 show players contesting\nthe delivery near goal, with a bright-green goalkeeper involved.\nIn images 15-16, the ball is away from the crowded goal area and players\nmove outward. Images 23 and 30 show subsequent play farther up the pitch,\nincluding a white-shirted player with the ball in image 30.\nLimits: The exact aerial contact and the player responsible for sending the\nball away are uncertain. Do not infer a goal from the delivery or goalkeeper\nmovement. The corner identification rests on the visible corner-arc setup,\nnot on a defensive wall or merely crowded player positions.",
      "message_content": "BEGIN DEMONSTRATION 2 \u2014 30 ORDERED IMAGES\nEvent: Corner kick.\nImage 10 shows a dark-shirted player approaching a stationary ball in the\ncorner arc beside the corner flag, where the goal line meets the touchline.\nImages 4 and 9 show dark-shirted attackers and white-shirted defenders\npositioned around the penalty area. Images 11-13 show players contesting\nthe delivery near goal, with a bright-green goalkeeper involved.\nIn images 15-16, the ball is away from the crowded goal area and players\nmove outward. Images 23 and 30 show subsequent play farther up the pitch,\nincluding a white-shirted player with the ball in image 30.\nLimits: The exact aerial contact and the player responsible for sending the\nball away are uncertain. Do not infer a goal from the delivery or goalkeeper\nmovement. The corner identification rests on the visible corner-arc setup,\nnot on a defensive wall or merely crowded player positions.\nEND DEMONSTRATION 2\n",
